# UI I18n JSON Is Mandatory

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L1 core UI rule.

## Use This When

- Keep this rule active for any new or changed user-facing UI text.

## Stop Here If

- Stop here once the translation-key and JSON-catalog policy is clear.

## Descend To

- No sibling descent required. Apply the rule directly to touched UI text.

## Policy

- Any new or changed user-facing UI text MUST use a translation key.
- Keys MUST be added to JSON catalogs in `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/` (not inline TS objects).
- Do not hardcode UI strings directly in TS/TSX (except test-only fixtures).

## Catalog location

- All translation catalogs are centralized in `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/<domain>/`.
- For Platform Space Settings flow use:
  - `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/platform/space-settings.en.json`
  - `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/platform/space-settings.es.json`
- For Author admin use:
  - `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/author/admin.en.json`
  - `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/author/admin.es.json`
- For Notifications email templates use:
  - `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/notifications/messages.en.json`
  - `packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/notifications/messages.es.json`

## Key format

- Use flat dotted keys: `"domain.section.key": "value"` — NO nested JSON objects.

## Required implementation steps for UI changes

1. Add translation key(s) to EN and ES JSON catalogs.
2. Use translator lookups in UI code (`t('...')`) instead of literals.
3. Keep interpolation in message templates (for example `{spaceLabel}`).
4. Ensure new keys are present in both locales before merging.

## Validation checklist

- No new hardcoded user-facing strings in touched UI components.
- Both locale JSON files include the same key set for new keys.
- Fallback behavior remains deterministic (EN fallback).
- `bun run --cwd packages/i18n-catalogs validate` passes for catalog parity and flat-key validation.
- `bun run --cwd packages/i18n-catalogs test` passes for catalog structure and locale parity coverage.

## Related rules

- `ui-i18n-direct-keys`: pass literal keys directly to `t(...)`; no key indirection.
